<Title>
	<Text Locale="US">ReferenceClock.prj</Text>
</Title>
<Description>
	<Text Locale="US">This example shows how to use reference clocks.  Select a clock source and a clock frequency and start the generation to phase lock the sample clock to the reference clock and begin generating.   You can also route the reference clock out.

Note:  The PCI-5421 has an onboard reference clock that is intended to be shared among multiple devices.  To share the onboard reference clock, press the Route Onboard Ref Clk To RTSI 7 button and select RTSI 7 as your reference clock source and 10MHz as your reference clock frequency on all modules you wish to synchronize.</Text>
</Description>
